ng\nflash flooding in and around the Gold Mountain Burn Scar.\n\nSOURCE...Public reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nGold Mountain Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nHighway 550 from Portland to Ouray and over the Gold Mountain burn\nscar.","ends":"2026-09-17T03:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Gunnison, CO; Hinsdale, CO; Ouray, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.73f0b275b56d4aba42806388f0ca716585d67d6f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.73f0b275b56d4aba42806388f0ca716585d67d6f.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 16 at 9:39AM MDT until September 18 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River,\nNorthwest San Juan Mountains, San Juan River Basin and Southwest\nSan Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nThis also includes the Gold Mountain, Elk and Ferris burn scars as\nwell as areas of steep, susceptible terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Recent heavy rainfall in southwest Colorado has led to already\nsaturated ground. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday afternoon through Thursday\nevening producing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash\nflooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-18T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d0f7f9a5a0805fda6f1988fda5f919f56cf2d735.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d0f7f9a5a0805fda6f1988fda5f919f56cf2d735.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-17T04:50:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 170450 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1050 PM MDT Wed Sep 16 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flash flooding will be possible for the coming days as record moisture propagates through eastern Utah and western Colorado. - Flood Watches remain in effect for SE Utah and SW Colorado today through Thursday. - Impacts from flash flooding could observed ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-16T18:50:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Sub-tropical moisture continues to propagate through the area which is feeding shower and thunderstorm activity through the end of the week. These storms bring a threat of heavy rainfall and potential for excess runoff, especially over burn scars. Because widespread wetting rainfall is expected over the next several days, the threat of critical fire weather conditions is eliminated ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"rgw01","station_name":"Ridgway","distance_km":5.6,"soil_temp_5cm_f":61.3,"soil_temp_15cm_f":62.44,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":0.02,"wind_speed_mph":2.87,"air_temp_f":54.77,"relative_humidity":0.946,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/rgw01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KMTJ","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KMTJ 170453Z AUTO 21006KT 10SM SCT075 BKN100 BKN120 16/14 A3036 RMK AO2 RAE06 SLP211 P0000 T01610144","temp_f":61,"wind_dir":210,"wind_kt":6,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"BKN","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1028.2,"observed":1789620780,"raw_taf":"TAF KMTJ 162321Z 1700/1724 13006KT P6SM VCSH SCT060 BKN090 PROB30 1700/170